# Session runs are machine OUTPUT, written per run. `demo_runs/` is a committed
# sample; `drop_runs/` is whatever this machine has produced locally.
drop_runs/
services/concept-portfolio/.env

# Every env file, everywhere — not just the one the panel writes.
#
# This used to name `services/concept-portfolio/.env` and nothing else, which
# covered the file the provider-key route creates and left every other way of
# holding a credential exposed: `apps/web/.env.local` is what Next reads on
# `next dev`, and a key pasted there would have been committed. A credential
# must not depend on remembering to add a line here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
